{"id":"mahabharata-3-090","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":90,"title":"नवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 90 · Lomasha joins the pilgrimage","summary":{"en":"Lomasha delivers Arjuna's request that he lead Yudhishthira to the holy places, and Indra's assurance that Arjuna will return. Yudhishthira rejoices, sends away most of his followers, and after three nights in the Kamyaka sets out with Lomasha, Dhaumya and a few Brahmins.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಪುಣ್ಯಕ್ಷೇತ್ರಗಳಿಗೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯೆಂಬ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಕೋರಿಕೆಯನ್ನೂ ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಮರಳುವನೆಂಬ ಇಂದ್ರನ ಭರವಸೆಯನ್ನೂ ಲೋಮಶರು ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಹರ್ಷಿಸಿ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿನ ಅನುಯಾಯಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕಳುಹಿಸಿ, ಕಾಮ್ಯಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಮೂರು ರಾತ್ರಿ ಕಳೆದು ಲೋಮಶ, ಧೌಮ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಕೆಲವು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"लोमश अर्जुन का यह अनुरोध सुनाते हैं कि वे युधिष्ठिर को पवित्र स्थानों पर ले जाएँ, और इन्द्र का आश्वासन कि अर्जुन लौटेंगे। युधिष्ठिर प्रसन्न होकर अधिकांश अनुयायियों को विदा करते हैं और काम्यक में तीन रातें बिताकर लोमश, धौम्य और कुछ ब्राह्मणों के साथ निकलते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుని పుణ్యక్షేత్రాలకు తీసుకువెళ్లమనే అర్జునుని కోరికను, అర్జునుడు తిరిగివస్తాడనే ఇంద్రుని భరోసాను లోమశుడు తెలియజేస్తాడు. యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఆనందించి చాలామంది అనుచరులను పంపివేసి, కామ్యకంలో మూడు రాత్రులు గడిపి లోమశుడు, ధౌమ్యుడు, కొద్దిమంది బ్రాహ్మణులతో బయలుదేరుతాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரரைப் புனிதத் தலங்களுக்கு அழைத்துச் செல்லுமாறு அர்ஜுனனின் வேண்டுகோளையும், அர்ஜுனன் திரும்புவான் என்ற இந்திரனின் உறுதியையும் லோமஶர் தெரிவிக்கிறார். யுதிஷ்டிரர் மகிழ்ந்து பெரும்பாலான பின்பற்றுவோரை அனுப்பி, காம்யகத்தில் மூன்று இரவுகள் தங்கிப் பின் லோமஶர், தௌம்யர், சில அந்தணர்களுடன் புறப்படுகிறார்.","ml":"അർജുനന്റെ അഭ്യർത്ഥന ലോമശൻ അറിയിക്കുന്നു: പുണ്യസ്ഥലങ്ങളിലൂടെ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ നയിക്കണം; അർജുനൻ മടങ്ങിവരുമെന്ന് ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ ഉറപ്പും. യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ സന്തോഷിക്കുന്നു, അനുയായികളിൽ മിക്കവരെയും തിരിച്ചയക്കുന്നു; കാമ്യകവനത്തിൽ മൂന്നു രാത്രി കഴിഞ്ഞശേഷം ലോമശൻ, ധൗമ്യൻ, കുറച്ച് ബ്രാഹ്മണർ എന്നിവരോടൊപ്പം പുറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.90; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"धनंजयेन चाप्युक्तं यत्तच्छृणु युधिष्ठिर ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं भ्रातरं मे योजयेर्धर्म्यया श्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, hear also what Dhananjaya said: \"Join my brother Yudhishthira to righteous prosperity."}},{"n":2,"text":"त्वं हि धर्मान्परान्वेत्थ तपांसि च तपोधन ।\nश्रीमतां चापि जानासि राज्ञां धर्मं सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Rich in austerity, you know the highest dharmas and the austerities, and you also know the eternal dharma of glorious kings."}},{"n":3,"text":"स भवान्यत्परं वेद पावनं पुरुषान्प्रति ।\nतेन संयोजयेथास्त्वं तीर्थपुण्येन पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So whatever you know to be the highest means of purification for men, join the Pandava to the merit of the holy fords by that."}},{"n":4,"text":"यथा तीर्थानि गच्छेत गाश्च दद्यात्स पार्थिवः ।\nतथा सर्वात्मना कार्यमिति मां विजयोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Vijaya told me that it must be arranged with all one's heart that the king visits the fords and gives away cows."}},{"n":5,"text":"भवता चानुगुप्तोऽसौ चरेत्तीर्थानि सर्वशः ।\nरक्षोभ्यो रक्षितव्यश्च दुर्गेषु विषमेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Guarded by you, let him wander to all the fords, and let him be protected from rakshasas in hard and rough places."}},{"n":6,"text":"दधीच इव देवेन्द्रं यथा चाप्यङ्गिरा रविम् ।\nतथा रक्षस्व कौन्तेयं राक्षसेभ्यो द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As Dadhicha guarded Indra and as Angiras guarded the sun, best of brahmins, so guard the son of Kunti from the rakshasas."}},{"n":7,"text":"यातुधाना हि बहवो राक्षसाः पर्वतोपमाः ।\nत्वयाभिगुप्तान्कौन्तेयान्नातिवर्तेयुरन्तिकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Many demons and rakshasas as big as mountains roam there, but they will not come near the Kunti's sons when you guard them.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"सोऽहमिन्द्रस्य वचनान्नियोगादर्जुनस्य च ।\nरक्षमाणो भयेभ्यस्त्वां चरिष्यामि त्वया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, at Indra's word and Arjuna's charge, I will travel with you, protecting you from dangers."}},{"n":9,"text":"द्विस्तीर्थानि मया पूर्वं दृष्टानि कुरुनन्दन ।\nइदं तृतीयं द्रक्ष्यामि तान्येव भवता सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Kuru, I have twice seen these fords before. With you I will see the same ones a third time."}},{"n":10,"text":"इयं राजर्षिभिर्याता पुण्यकृद्भिर्युधिष्ठिर ।\nमन्वादिभिर्महाराज तीर्थयात्रा भयापहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, this pilgrimage that removes fear was undertaken by royal sages of merit, Manu and others."}},{"n":11,"text":"नानृजुर्नाकृतात्मा च नावैद्यो न च पापकृत् ।\nस्नाति तीर्थेषु कौरव्य न च वक्रमतिर्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No crooked man, no one of unrefined self, no ignorant or sinful man, no man of twisted mind bathes at the fords, descendant of Kuru."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वं तु धर्ममतिर्नित्यं धर्मज्ञः सत्यसंगरः ।\nविमुक्तः सर्वपापेभ्यो भूय एव भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But you are always devoted to dharma, you know dharma and keep your word. Freed from all sins, you will rise higher still."}},{"n":13,"text":"यथा भगीरथो राजा राजानश्च गयादयः ।\nयथा ययातिः कौन्तेय तथा त्वमपि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As King Bhagiratha, and kings such as Gaya, and as Yayati did, Pandava, so will you."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"न हर्षात्संप्रपश्यामि वाक्यस्यास्योत्तरं क्वचित् ।\nस्मरेद्धि देवराजो यं किं नामाभ्यधिकं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In my joy I can find no reply to these words. Whom the king of the gods remembers, what could be greater than that?"}},{"n":15,"text":"भवता संगमो यस्य भ्राता यस्य धनंजयः ।\nवासवः स्मरते यस्य को नामाभ्यधिकस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What could be greater than being joined with you, and having Dhananjaya as a brother, and being remembered by Vasava?"}},{"n":16,"text":"यच्च मां भगवानाह तीर्थानां दर्शनं प्रति ।\nधौम्यस्य वचनादेषा बुद्धिः पूर्वं कृतैव मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And as for what you, revered sir, say about visiting the fords, I had already formed that intention on Dhaumya's word."}},{"n":17,"text":"तद्यदा मन्यसे ब्रह्मन्गमनं तीर्थदर्शने ।\nतदैव गन्तास्मि दृढमेष मे निश्चयः परः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So whenever you think it right, brahmin, I will go to see the fords. This is my firm and final resolve."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"गमने कृतबुद्धिं तं पाण्डवं लोमशोऽब्रवीत् ।\nलघुर्भव महाराज लघुः स्वैरं गमिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"To the Pandava, who had set his mind on going, Lomasha said: \"Be light, great king. Light, you will travel as you please.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"बिक्षाभुजो निवर्तन्तां ब्राह्मणा यतयश्च ये ।\nये चाप्यनुगताः पौरा राजभक्तिपुरस्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the brahmins who live on alms and the ascetics turn back, and also the townsfolk who have followed out of loyalty to the king."}},{"n":20,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रं महाराजमभिगच्छन्तु चैव ते ।\nस दास्यति यथाकालमुचिता यस्य या भृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let them go to the great king Dhritarashtra, who will give each of them in due time the support they deserve."}},{"n":21,"text":"स चेद्यथोचितां वृत्तिं न दद्यान्मनुजेश्वरः ।\nअस्मत्प्रियहितार्थाय पाञ्चाल्यो वः प्रदास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And if that lord of men does not give them fitting maintenance, then the Panchala prince will give it to you, for our welfare and pleasure."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो भूयिष्ठशः पौरा गुरुभारसमाहिताः ।\nविप्राश्च यतयो युक्ता जग्मुर्नागपुरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then most of the townsfolk, weighed down by heavy burdens, and the brahmins and ascetics, went off toward Hastinapura."}},{"n":23,"text":"तान्सर्वान्धर्मराजस्य प्रेम्णा राजाम्बिकासुतः ।\nप्रतिजग्राह विधिवद्धनैश्च समतर्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Ambika, the king Dhritarashtra, out of affection for the king of dharma, received all of them properly and satisfied them with wealth."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः कुन्तीसुतो राजा लघुभिर्ब्राह्मणैः सह ।\nलोमशेन च सुप्रीतस्त्रिरात्रं काम्यकेऽवसत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Kunti, the king, in the company of a few brahmins and of Lomasha, stayed three nights at Kamyaka, very pleased."}}]}]}